  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two thermodynamical process are shown in the figure. The molar heat capacity for process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math>. The molar heat capacity at constant pressure and constant volume are represented by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></math>, respectively. Choose the correct statement.</p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4c085d90-f6f0-4a5e-b68e-ff6a65779362.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 256px;\"/>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "a4Bwq",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
